Steve,

Normally you want the DOS/FAT partition to be the first partition.  =
Various reasons for this, such as the bootloaders normally use part of the =
first cylinder and some of the filesystems do not play well with some =
bootloaders, some versions of DOS/FAT/console code have issues with =
partitions in the higher cylinder/sectors of some of the bigger hard =
drives, its a semi-standard, it makes it easier to switch bootloaders, =
etc. =20

I am not as familar with ARC.  All my systems use SRM.  IF you do not have =
a problem with the console seeing the partition and you can format it as =
DOS/FAT with the system files you should be alright.  Copy MILO onto this =
partition.  Set up the console to boot this partition.  Test boot to MILO =
without parameters and boot to linux manually.  Then shut down and set up =
the parameters.  Others here can help with the details or you can check =
out www.alphalinux.org there should be some references there to the =
neccessary details for UDB ARC configuration or you can check the archives =
of this list as it has been discussed before in both places. =20


Calvin.
Hope this helps.


