>>>fwupdate

it loads AlphaBIOS
and I've got a floppy with milo and linload.exe on it
and even a kernel built with use SRM as bootloader
turned off
about now AlphaBIOS hands it over to milo and milo
hangs on 

Calibrating Delay Loop 

Which I've seen before and it usually happens when
you've been messing with settings in AlphaBIOS and
you've just updated the environment (F10). This
problem was usually rectified (at least in my case) by
cold-booting the alpha, after that it would work just
fine(till i played with AlphaBIOS settings again)

So when I warm or cold boot said alpha it reverts back
to SRM(i guess this is a convience feature such that
you don't get screwed by firmware that is non-working)

but I really want AlphaBIOS to stick because I have
faith that milo will work after a reboot. 

I have tried AlphaBIOS v 5.70 and 5.66-1
and several of the 2.0.X milos

any ideas ?
thanks 
greg
